description.narrative:
The overall objective of this contribution is improved economic sustainability and business development of Serbian digital media, information and communications sector stakeholders.
Specific objectives are:
1. Implementation of business and technological development. Improvement of beneficiaries’ capacity;
2. Leverage of project funds with third party funds (commercial or development assistance partners) to incentivize firm-level investments, or secure better access to loans for beneficiaries;
3. Improve beneficiaries' access to finance and investment readiness and
4. Outline of the design and investment partnerships for the establishment of a stand-alone Fund for Media, Information and Digital Environment Innovation.

Key results achieved include:

Business and Technological Development:

- The project supported nine media and media-adjacent organizations with 10 grants, guiding their transformation through expert deployment and structural redesign. The beneficiary cohort, as of August 2024, included legacy media (FoNet, Vreme, Boom93, 021), media-adjacent ICT companies (AI Software, Just Start), digital media (June Vesti), and new media actors (Podcast Podrska, Agelast podcast, Tampon Zona podcast, Biznis Price podcast, Podmedia);

- The cohort collectively surpassed $8.6 million in total revenue from the start of the Mediji.Inovacije project. Impact revenue generated by the cohort totalled $808,608, with 65% contributed by new media partners;

- Vreme, one of the oldest privately owned independent media outlets, expanded its digital product portfolio with two newsletters (one gained over 1,000 subscribers), launched a new website, established a digitally-focused newsroom, and integrated modern ad technology and payment systems. Its monthly revenue from display ads and subscriptions grew from zero/minimal in January 2022 to over $2,000 by mid-2024;

- FoNet, a national news agency, completed a year-long business transformation grant, leading to a 63.9% increase in total revenue and a 39.21% increase in clients. They established new business departments, launched an updated website with a new brand logo, and conducted an advertising campaign to enhance market presence;

- Tampon Zona (TZ), a podcast promoting women's empowerment, generated $29,845 from commercial contracts and secured 12 sponsorship deals. Merchandise sales brought in an additional $16,893, representing an approximate 50% return on investment from the Mediji.Inovacije grant. Its YouTube subscribers exceeded 22,000, and its total social media follower base grew by 727%;

- Podmedia secured $36,400 in revenue from sponsorships, events, and studio rental fees, equivalent to 72.8% of the grant received. A founders investment of $25,000 further contributed to its financial stability;

- Podkast Podrka increased its revenue to over $100,000 during the grant period, establishing 22 new partnerships and products/services;

- Boom93 expanded into seven new markets, engaged a team of correspondents, introduced geolocation technologies, and saw a 30.47% increase in visitors and a 49.92% increase in pageviews on its redesigned portal;

- The Joint Revenue Stream (JRS) Network in the South launched a centralized sales platform, earning $16,555 by April 2024. The networks total user count increased by 33.9% year-over-year;

- The Vojvodina Media Network (VMN) in the North led to the formation of a regional media network, increasing market share and revenue generation, adding nearly 10,000 new users, and producing a 20.3% growth in social media followers;

- Alesto AS secured sponsorships generating up to $11,000 monthly, including a 12-month contract for $7,200 per month. Its YouTube channel recorded 1.5 million views in April 2024;

- AI Integration: The project advanced with familiarizing its cohort with AI, conducting ChatGPT training for Boom93 staff, featuring AI discussions at the "Digitalk: Media Days" conference, and organizing a masterclass on AI regulation with SHARE Foundation and academic institutions. Support was also provided to FoNet, Tampon Zona, and Glas umadije to integrate AI into operational workflows, improving promotional activities and efficiency;

- A Talent and Media Innovation Network was launched to promote youth involvement in Serbias independent media scene.

Leverage of Funds and Access to Finance (A2F):

- The project mobilized $584,328 in leveraged investment, of which 91% originated from the private sector;

- Beneficiaries accessed $158,964 in commercial finance, including two collateral-backed loans. The collateral-backed loan mechanism was an innovative scheme introduced to mitigate lender risk and expand access to capital for independent media outlets. Through this mechanism, Just Start secured a $10,000 loan. In addition, FoNet obtained two commercial loans with project support: $48,000 to refinance and restructure existing debt and $25,000 to stabilize shortterm cash flow. June vesti secured a fixedinterest credit line of up to $43,000;

- While the planned Access to Finance (A2F) digital marketplace was not realised, this gap was partially filled through the establishment of an investment fund managed by the Media Development Investment Fund (MDIF), providing new financing options to Serbia's media sector.

Gender Equality and Social Inclusion (GESI):

- Investments in training and analytical tools (SmartOcto) enabled the production of more gender-sensitive content;

- Eight GESI- and youth-focused training sessions were delivered, contributing to a substaintial increase in gender-responsive and youth-related reporting, from 335 to 685 articles per month;

- A Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) was signed with the Feminist Cultural Center BeFem, facilitating collaboration on GESI themes and the co-organization of the Women.Innovation.Media event.
